# TubeFetch v1.0.1

Your complete desktop solution for managing and archiving YouTube channels. TubeFetch is a powerful desktop application designed for content creators, archivists, and YouTube power-users who want a reliable way to download videos and shorts from their favorite channels.

Built with the speed and reliability of `yt-dlp` and a clean, intuitive interface, TubeFetch streamlines the entire process of saving content locally.

![App Screenshot](https://i.imgur.com/your-screenshot-url.png)
*(**Pro Tip:** Take a screenshot of TubeFetch running, upload it to a site like [Imgur](https://imgur.com/), and replace the URL above to showcase your app!)*

## Why TubeFetch?

Tired of manually checking your favorite YouTube channels for new content or using unreliable web-based downloaders? TubeFetch brings all the functionality you need to your desktop in a single, robust application. It remembers what you've already downloaded, supports both long-form videos and Shorts, and gives you full control over save locations and video quality.

## Key Features

*   🗂️ **Multi-Channel Management:** Add, remove, and manage an unlimited list of YouTube channels in one place.
*   🎬 **Dual Download Modes:** Independently download the latest **long-form videos** or the latest **Shorts** from any channel.
*   🧠 **Smart Search & History:** The app keeps a history of your downloads for each channel and will only fetch videos that are new since your last check. Never download the same video twice!
*   🍪 **Full Cookie Support:** By providing your browser's cookies, you can download age-restricted, private, or members-only content that you have access to.
*   📂 **Flexible Save Locations:** Set a global download folder for all channels, or override it and give each channel its own unique save location.
*   🎨 **Light & Dark Themes:** Choose the look that fits your style with easily switchable light and dark modes.
*   🔄 **Backup & Restore:** Export your entire channel list and download history to a single JSON file for easy backup or migration to another computer.

