## Installation

1.  Go to the [**Releases Page**](https://github.com/your-username/TubeFetch/releases) of this repository.
2.  Download the `TubeFetch_v1.0.1_installer.exe` file from the latest release.
3.  Run the installer and follow the on-screen instructions.

## How to Use

#### Adding a Channel
1.  Click the **+ Add Channel** button.
2.  Paste the URL of a YouTube channel (e.g., `https://www.youtube.com/@MrBeast`).
3.  Click **Add Channel**. The app will fetch the channel's details and add it to your list.

#### Downloading Videos
1.  Select a channel from the list on the left.
2.  In the "Download Controls" panel, enter the **number** of new videos you want to search for.
3.  Choose the content **Type** (`Videos` or `Shorts`).
4.  Select your desired **Resolution** (e.g., 1080p).
5.  Click the **Download** button!

### Using Cookies for Private Content

1.  Install a browser extension that can export cookies in **Netscape** format (e.g., [Get cookies.txt LOCALLY](https://chrome.google.com/webstore/detail/get-cookiestxt-locally/jjlcamleiafcjlcikddoceicomdloiad)).
2.  Navigate to YouTube.com and export your cookies using the extension.
3.  In TubeFetch, go to **Settings** -> **YouTube Cookie Settings**.
4.  Paste the entire content of your Netscape cookie file into the text box.
5.  Click **Save Cookies**. The app will now use your login session for all future requests.

